#fields	indicator	indicator_type	meta.source	meta.desc	meta.url
decepticon-telemetry-gateway.purpleailab.workers.dev	Intel::DOMAIN	threatdefence-decepticon	Decepticon high: Decepticon usage telemetry gateway (Cloudflare Worker forwarding to PostHog). Shipped in the launcher's .env template; the setup wizard defaults to sharing (DECEPTICON_TELEMETRY=research) unless the operator declines (clients/launcher/cmd/onboard.go:280,916). POST /v1/telemetry from the langgraph container. Seen from your network, Decepticon ran from your network (Decepticon operators)	https://github.com/BitterSecurity/Decepticon/blob/6b15092d2e0b41f2ef5af79a16333582cc3fb353/clients/launcher/internal/config/env.example#L200
decepticon-telemetry/1.0	Intel::SOFTWARE	threatdefence-decepticon	Decepticon high: User agent of Decepticon's telemetry exporter on POST /v1/telemetry to its gateway. Visible only with TLS inspection (Decepticon operators)	https://github.com/BitterSecurity/Decepticon/blob/6b15092d2e0b41f2ef5af79a16333582cc3fb353/packages/decepticon/decepticon/telemetry/exporter.py#L35
decepticon-roe/1	Intel::SOFTWARE	threatdefence-decepticon	Decepticon high: User agent of Decepticon's passive subdomain discovery, which queries https://crt.sh/?q=%.<root>&output=json when an engagement is created (passive_discovery.py:71). Sent to crt.sh, never to the target. Visible only with TLS inspection (Decepticon operators)	https://github.com/BitterSecurity/Decepticon/blob/6b15092d2e0b41f2ef5af79a16333582cc3fb353/packages/decepticon/decepticon/passive_discovery.py#L40
decepticon-http-sandbox/1	Intel::SOFTWARE	threatdefence-decepticon	Decepticon high: User agent of the HTTP client that sends every agent command to the Decepticon sandbox daemon (POST /execute, /execute_tmux and others on port 9999). Normally on a Docker bridge network; crosses your network only when the sandbox is remote (Decepticon operators)	https://github.com/BitterSecurity/Decepticon/blob/6b15092d2e0b41f2ef5af79a16333582cc3fb353/packages/decepticon/decepticon/backends/http_transport.py#L139
Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Decepticon/1.0)	Intel::SOFTWARE	threatdefence-decepticon	Decepticon medium: Default user agent of Decepticon's http_recon helper. The helper is in the package but not bound to any agent at 6b15092d or v2.2.2, so expect it only from forks or plugins (Decepticon operators)	https://github.com/BitterSecurity/Decepticon/blob/6b15092d2e0b41f2ef5af79a16333582cc3fb353/packages/decepticon/decepticon/tools/network/protocols.py#L84
Decepticon/1.0	Intel::SOFTWARE	threatdefence-decepticon	Decepticon medium: User agent Decepticon's LiteLLM gateway sends to the Vercel AI Gateway for the vercel/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5 model entry only. Visible only with TLS inspection (Decepticon operators)	https://github.com/BitterSecurity/Decepticon/blob/6b15092d2e0b41f2ef5af79a16333582cc3fb353/config/litellm.yaml#L622
codex_cli_rs/0.0.0 (Unknown 0; unknown) unknown	Intel::SOFTWARE	threatdefence-decepticon	Decepticon medium: Placeholder user agent Decepticon's LiteLLM handler sends to chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex when it runs on a ChatGPT subscription (originator codex_cli_rs). The real Codex CLI sends its version and OS. Override: CHATGPT_USER_AGENT. Visible only with TLS inspection (Decepticon operators)	https://github.com/BitterSecurity/Decepticon/blob/6b15092d2e0b41f2ef5af79a16333582cc3fb353/config/codex_chatgpt_handler.py#L54
